From 92d3d7cab10e6a933d0a2da46657b2e41708e4ac Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 08:43:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 36/59] Different-subject disagreements are competing evidence;
 contradiction follow-ups reach both sides; department round-robin routing

C1: a disagreement whose sides each name exactly one subject entity (service/component/issue/repo)
and different ones opens no conflict; both are committed and the gate's independence and
min_independent_units rules rank them (recorded as 'competing'); same-subject disagreements still open
conflicts. C2: contradiction follow-ups no longer route away from the holders behind both sides (as
documented). C3: the department diversity bonus decays per group; exact ties prefer unit holders.
Decision D19. From the dev analysis of the hardened run (all 17 failures were different-service claims
treated as a contradiction). Engineer: WP1 (claude-sonnet-5-5); full suite 518 passed, 7 skipped.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QgQYqiZ8KjrbuXgxGadraA
